 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The web app uses the process-wide `sessions` store in
+[`larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py). Volunteers asked for faster requests, so session reads
+and writes now use a dictionary in the web app process, removing the Postgres query from session access.
 
-## Shaped by
+## Known limits
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- Sessions disappear when the process restarts or is deployed; members must log in again.
+- Processes do not share sessions. In 2023, requests routed between two servers logged members out, and deploys
+  disrupted opening hours. With this store, run a single web app process or use sticky routing to keep each member's
+  requests on the same process. Sticky routing does not preserve sessions across restarts.
